'''''Trifolium glomeratum''''' is a species of [[clover]] known by the common names '''clustered clover'''<ref>{{PLANTS|id=TRGL4|taxon=Trifolium glomeratum|accessdate=15 December 2015}}</ref><ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> and '''bush clover'''.

== Description ==
It is an [[annual herb]] growing [[decumbent]] to upright in form with mostly hairless herbage. The leaves are made up of oval [[Leaflet (botany)|leaflets]] up to {{Convert|1.2|cm|frac=8|sp=us}} in length. The [[inflorescence]]s occur in [[leaf axils]], each a cluster of many flowers resembling a [[Pseudanthium|flowerhead]]. Each flower has a calyx of [[sepal]]s with triangular points that bend outward and a pink [[Corolla (botany)|corolla]].
==Distribution and habitat==
It is native to Eurasia and North Africa and it is known elsewhere as an [[introduced species]]. It easily takes hold in disturbed areas, becoming a common weed.

